    "title": "Panthers, Rangers to Play First NHL Outdoor Game in Florida",
    "text": "• The Florida Panthers will host the New York Rangers in the first outdoor NHL game in Florida at loanDepot Park, home of the Miami Marlins, on Friday.\n• The game is expected to have a sold-out crowd.\n• The retractable roof at loanDepot Park will be opened before the game.\n• The game is the first of two outdoor games in Florida this season; the Tampa Bay Lightning will host the Boston Bruins on February 1 at Raymond James Stadium.\n• The NHL played its All-Star Game in Tampa in 2018, which sparked the idea of outdoor games in Florida.\n• The ice-making process involves custom refrigeration units, coolant, aluminum trays, and a water-soluble paint to whiten the ice.\n• The ice sheet will be about 25% thicker than usual.\n• The rink used for the Panthers-Rangers game will be moved to Tampa after Friday's game.\n• The Panthers were one of two teams that had never played in an outdoor game before this.\n• The Rangers have a 5-0-0 record in outdoor games.\n• loanDepot Park will be the 15th Major League Baseball stadium to host an outdoor game.\n• This will be the 44th outdoor game in NHL history.\n• The warmest game-time temperature in NHL outdoor game history was 65 degrees (18 Celsius) in Denver in 2016.\n• Two golf carts will be used to transport the goalies from the ice to the locker rooms.\n• Brad Marchand will be playing in his fourth outdoor game.\n• Sergei Bobrovsky will be setting a record for the longest span between outdoor game appearances.\n• Paul Maurice will be coaching an outdoor game for the third time.",
